        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1830">

                <pb facs="1195" n="1079" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg1079"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 816.001Q4/1.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister of
                        Salvador.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 3, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 23rd ultimo, with which you enclose an autograph
                    letter from Dr. Alfonso Quiñonez M., announcing to the President his assumption
                    of the Chief Magistracy of the Republic of Salvador, by reason of the leave of
                    absence granted to Señor Don Carlos Melendez by the National Assembly.</p>
                <p>I have taken pleasure in forwarding the letter to the President, whose reply will
                    be delivered through the American Minister at San Salvador.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
